Proxmox VE
  Proxion's API client (packages/pve-api) is generated from an API schema
  extracted from Proxmox VE's own documentation (pve-docs / the PVE API
  viewer). Proxion is an independent, unofficial project and is not
  affiliated with or endorsed by Proxmox Server Solutions GmbH.
  https://pve.proxmox.com/wiki/Proxmox_VE_API
  https://github.com/proxmox/pve-docs

noVNC
  Proxion's embedded VM/CT console speaks the same RFB-over-websocket
  protocol PVE's own noVNC-based console uses, and the browser-side
  console component is built on noVNC.
  License: Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL-2.0)
  https://github.com/novnc/noVNC

xterm.js
  Proxion's embedded node/container terminal is built on xterm.js.
  License: MIT
  https://github.com/xtermjs/xterm.js

uPlot
  Proxion's resource graphs (CPU/memory/disk/network over time) are built
  on uPlot.
  License: MIT
  https://github.com/leeoniya/uPlot

pngjs
  Proxion's server encodes console thumbnails (captured over VNC) as PNG
  with pngjs.
  License: MIT
  https://github.com/pngjs/pngjs

Josefin Sans, Open Sans
  Proxion's display (titles/big figures/the wordmark) and UI/body typefaces
  -- including identifiers (UPIDs, MACs, volume IDs, etc.), which render in
  Open Sans rather than a shipped monospace face -- self-hosted via
  @fontsource-variable/josefin-sans and @fontsource-variable/open-sans.
  Monospace is used only for the terminal and the task-log line viewer, via
  the end user's own installed system monospace font (no webfont shipped).
  License: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (OFL-1.1)
  https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Josefin+Sans
  https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Open+Sans

